{"id": "EUVD-2026-80306", "enisaUuid": "177c6a83-47e9-3e27-9b10-c416b5d31888", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfs/ntfs3: fix out-of-bounds read of INDEX_ROOT in reparse/objid init\n\nntfs_reparse_init() and ntfs_objid_init() parse the index root of the\n$Extend/$Reparse and $Extend/$ObjId metafiles (the INDEX_ROOT attributes\nnamed $R and $O). They read its type and rule fields through\nresident_data(), which does not check that the resident attribute is\nlarge enough to hold them.\n\nmi_enum_attr() accepts a resident attribute with data_off == asize and\ndata_size == 0. For such an attribute placed last in its MFT record,\nresident_data() returns a pointer to the end of the record_size buffer,\nso reading root->type / root->rule reads past the allocation.\n\nUse resident_data_ex(attr, sizeof(struct INDEX_ROOT)) and bail out when\nit returns NULL, as ntfs_security_init() already does for $SDH / $SII.\n\nThe attribute is only parsed while mounting a crafted image, so this\nneeds CAP_SYS_ADMIN.\n\n BUG: KASAN: slab-out-of-bounds in ntfs_reparse_init (fs/ntfs3/fsntfs.c:2306)\n Read of size 4 at addr ffff88801219dc00 by task mount\n  ntfs_reparse_init (fs/ntfs3/fsntfs.c:2306)\n  ntfs_fill_super (fs/ntfs3/super.c:1604)\n  get_tree_bdev_flags (fs/super.c:1703)\n  vfs_get_tree (fs/super.c:1758)\n  path_mount (fs/namespace.c:4131)\n  __x64_sys_mount (fs/namespace.c:4360)", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T08:48:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:52:38", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eb80003744e32a7366a523015e4acfe0a2ac7d88", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bd631e2005290a55c8edda87363bc0d594c01705", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/94fce1d3e74fe011e21f17490ba58491709fd7e5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/66c074eab6f966fbe48a0fc4b3a45b2a2e2df527", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/64bb6000bfbdf241a6dd578199acd90321a4243e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/72caafbc95c5dca8266a942b8e96ad81d8d9adc7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2064bc663f89e61b8681c1fb9d1ce445de72063d"], "aliases": ["GHSA-683x-gqv7-78pp", "CVE-2026-89785"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "38d0ddef-e51d-32c5-bcff-4dc70c3da0cd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "4b49496f-1152-39ac-bd61-7f4e9348ac08", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "5f82f7e8-1764-3808-a6a2-b9bab92b6f0f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82cae269cfa953032fbb8980a7d554d60fb00b17 <94fce1d3e74fe011e21f17490ba58491709fd7e5"}, {"id": "7050de22-6192-3218-82d8-ad497e4e3e1a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "782cd5a3-41e3-36c1-8df3-96d3195fdb4d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82cae269cfa953032fbb8980a7d554d60fb00b17 <64bb6000bfbdf241a6dd578199acd90321a4243e"}, {"id": "922039e7-cb46-33bf-975d-20753044d177", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82cae269cfa953032fbb8980a7d554d60fb00b17 <72caafbc95c5dca8266a942b8e96ad81d8d9adc7"}, {"id": "a29b7e24-1e6b-337e-97b4-9bb2f4e6dcda", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82cae269cfa953032fbb8980a7d554d60fb00b17 <66c074eab6f966fbe48a0fc4b3a45b2a2e2df527"}, {"id": "a2c03575-a4c0-3e9c-b591-8f1a3473a945", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82cae269cfa953032fbb8980a7d554d60fb00b17 <2064bc663f89e61b8681c1fb9d1ce445de72063d"}, {"id": "aadd13a1-c106-33ad-9b58-5e5a2a2dcde3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "b7bc8dfd-8ee2-3916-bac9-a4ed8629c1db", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "c0b95597-470d-3b80-8c0